# Milestone: M3
# Covers: modules loaded into a Realm do not pollute other Realms; bindings
#         from module are visible only in the Realm where it was loaded.
#
# blocked: `import "name" as Alias` module-load surface not shipped — the
#          lexer/parser have no `import` keyword and there is no import-table
#          registration, so the chk-host-driver (which can already create
#          isolated realms; see realm_isolation.chk) has no way to load a
#          module into one realm and check its bindings are absent from
#          another.  This is the import-table gap, not the multi-realm gap.
# matrix-row: chunk-lifecycle-realm
#
# Reason: import-table registration and module-loading surface via
# urbi_vm_import_register land at M6 (stdlib). At M3, urbi_load_chunk
# is a stub that returns URBI_ERR_NOTIMP.
#
# When M6 lands, implement this fixture by setting up two Realms, loading a
# module into one, and verifying bindings from that module are not visible
# in the other Realm.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at M6, requires host-driver setup):
#   [Create r1 and r2]
#   import "foo" as F;  [in r1]
#   [Verify F is bound in r1 but not in r2]
